BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Planning
DESCRIPTION:The Buncombe County Pedestrian Plan Steering Committee is a new
  advisory group that will help shape the vision\, goals\, and strategies o
 f the plan. The plan will focus on creating a connected network of sidewal
 ks\, crosswalks\, and safe walking routes that link neighborhoods to schoo
 ls\, job centers\, parks\, and other essential destinations. Members will 
 review public input and draft recommendations and ensure the plan reflects
  the voices of Buncombe County residents. https://www.buncombenc.gov/calen
 dar.aspx?EID=9883
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T121500
DTSTAMP;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T105527
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T110000
LAST-MODIFIED;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T105527
LOCATION: -     
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pedestrian Plan Steering Committee Meeting
UID:9883
URL:/common/modules/iCalendar/iCalendar.aspx?feed=calendar&catID=37
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Planning
DESCRIPTION:The Buncombe County Board of Commissioners appointed 13 members
  and 2 alternates to serve on the Swannanoa Plan Steering Committee. This 
 Committee is crucial to the success of the planning process for the Swanna
 noa Small Area Plan\, bringing their knowledge of the community\, expertis
 e in a focus area\, interest in the future of Swannanoa\, and willingness 
 to help create a vision for the long term.  https://www.buncombenc.gov/cal
 endar.aspx?EID=8807
